# §6: unit_make_adder_activation.lm2 under --walk-methods. T6b builds the node from the host's
# walked activation as it is at the return: n changed before it, k a field the host declares, u a
# formal addN never names -- the node carries n and k, not u. add7(1)=7, add100(1)=100, add7(1)=7.
# Mutants: the constructor's own capture store dropped (an Entry other than 7 or a crash) --
# l2_emit_mad_construct_one's per-capture store call, not the count/emit passes themselves.
fn: makeAdder (int: n; int: u) fn: (int: x) int
    n: n + 1
    int: k (n * 2)
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + k + x
    return: addN

add7: makeAdder 1 9
add100: makeAdder 32 9
int: a (add7: 1)
int: b (add100: 1)
int: c (add7: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 7 && b = 100 && c = 7
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
